  "lineage": "Traditional music of Galicia in north-west Spain, collected from the 1920s by the Seminario de Estudos Galegos and revived from the mid-1970s by Milladoiro and the pandereteira singing groups — the two-drone gaita galega leading muiñeiras in fast 6/8 and alalás in free rhythm, driven by rows of women singing in nasal parallel harmony over hand-struck pandeiretas and bombo, with hurdy-gurdy and later bouzouki filling harmony.",
